course: dictionary
lesson: 6574
title: Nightjar: a bird that hides in plain sight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a thing, like nightjar, and the sentence around them often tells you what that thing is like. «The nightjar, which frightened Toad in the night wood, is a bird that hunts moths at dusk.» The words after the comma tell you what kind of bird it is: one that hunts moths when the light fades.
explain: Look for clues in the rest of the sentence. «Makes a long churring sound like a little engine» tells you how the bird sounds. The simile, a little engine, helps you picture a sound you may never have heard. Try it: can you hear a machine that never stops?
explain: Some words explain how an animal stays safe. Camouflage means colours or shapes that help an animal hide. The nightjar's brown, speckled feathers look like bark and dead leaves, so it can sleep on the ground or along a branch in the day and be hard to spot.
fact: A nightjar is a brown, speckled bird.
fact: «Nightjar» means a bird that hunts moths at dusk and at night.
fact: Its long, whirring, churring song is one of its clues: you can hear it on summer nights.
fact: In the day it sleeps on the ground or along a branch, hidden by its camouflage.
fact: Nightjars come to Britain and Europe in summer from Africa; in North America, related birds are the whip-poor-will and nighthawk.
exercise: «The nightjar hunts moths at dusk.» What does a nightjar hunt? | Fish from the river | Mice in the barn | Worms in the garden | *Moths
exercise: Why is it hard to see a nightjar sleeping on the ground in the day? | It sings loudly all day. | *Its feathers look like bark and dead leaves, which is camouflage. | It is too big to hide. | It sleeps in deep water.
exercise: Find and copy the word that describes the sound the nightjar makes. | Toad | *churring | winter | nightjar
test: What does camouflage help an animal do? | *Hide | Fly to Africa | Run very fast | Sing loudly
test: Where do nightjars come from to spend the summer in Britain? | The bottom of the sea | Iceland | The north pole | *Africa
exam: Which clue tells you the nightjar is active when the light fades? | It flies to Africa for the winter | *It hunts moths at dusk | It is a bird | It frightened Toad
